timestamp=2026-11-04T12:47:48.221Z level=INFO run=3476ed77 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\ncomp = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/companies.csv')\ninv = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/invoices.csv')\n\n# These are buyer IDs that are not sellers, and also not in companies.csv - external entities\n# That matches (c) \"sellers whose payments to external recipients look outsized relative to their declared business footprint\"\n# But the question asks for \"companies whose profile or transaction history would merit deeper investigation\"\n# and to \"return a set of 10 company IDs that are most likely to require investigation\"\n# Companies - probably entities in the companies dataset (registered companies)\n# External buyer IDs (not in companies table) are not companies in the dataset's company registry. So we should focus on company IDs that exist in companies.csv\n\n# Let us re-score limiting to company_ids in companies.csv\nall_comp_ids = set(comp['company_id'].unique())\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
