timestamp=2026-11-04T12:49:24.671Z level=INFO run=3476ed77 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python << 'PY'\nimport pandas as pd\n\ncomp = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/companies.csv')\ninv = pd.read_csv('/app/dataset/invoices.csv')\n\n# From the patterns:\n# (a) unusual leading-digit behavior among active sellers - 8382, 4612 stand out (all same leading digit, many invoices). Also 6453 and 2029 are sellers with extreme behaviors.\n# (b) buyer-only companies with weak fundamentals - 7021, 8285, 4521, 8770, 1060, 3495, 8810 are all buyer-only, very small (16-36 employees), young bank accounts (1-4 months), recent-ish registration.\n# (c) sellers sending outsized payments to external recipients relative to footprint - 6453 (small, 36 emp, rev ~109k, sends ~373k total, mostly to external buyers not in companies.csv) and 2029 similar. Also 5009, 4327 have very high ratio outflow to declared revenue (rev very small, outflows much larger relative to rev).\n\nWe need 10 company IDs most likely to require investigation. The task states \"pay attention to patterns...\" and lists (a), (b), (c). The strongest red flags are:\n1. 6453 - seller, tiny company (36 emp) with rev ~109k but total outflows ~373k (ratio > 3), only 2 buyers, both external (not in companies). Very suspicious.\n2. 2029 - similar to 6453: small (34 emp), rev ~131k, outflows ~390k, only 2 buyers, both external. Suspicious.\n3. 7021 - buyer-only, weak (36 emp, bank acc 2 months, maybe region missing?), appears only as buyer despite profile that could be used to facilitate transactions.\n4. 8285 - buyer-only, weak (27 emp, bank acc 2 months).\n5. 4521 - buyer-only, weak (18 emp, bank acc 4 months).\n6. 8770 - buyer-only, weak (20 emp, bank acc 3 months).\n7. 1060 - buyer-only, weak (28 emp, bank acc 3 months).\n8. 3495 - buyer-only, weak (16 emp, bank acc 3 months) - smallest employees.\n9. 8810 - buyer-only, weak (18 emp, bank acc 1 month) - youngest bank account.\n10. 8382 - seller, extreme Benford anomaly (all amounts start with 1, many invoices), unusual pattern. Also 4612 same. Between them, 8382/4612 look like \"round number\" invoice mills.\n\nAlso 5009 and 4327 have high outflow/rev ratio but are large companies in employees? They have small declared revenue relative to outflows - could be significant. But compared to (a),(b),(c) patterns, the buyer-only weak companies and the external-recipient heavy sellers are clearest.\n\nLet us pick top 10 that cover all three categories clearly: include 6453, 2029 (c); include the 7 buyer-only weak ones (b); and include one of 8382/4612 (a) as the 10th.\n\nThe buyer-only weak ones are 7 total: 7021, 8285, 4521, 8770, 1060, 3495, 8810. That’s 7. Plus 6453, 2029 = 9. Need 1 more - pick 8382 (most extreme Benford anomaly, large seller with many small identical-amount invoices). That gives 10.\n\nSo the set is {6453, 2029, 7021, 8285, 4521, 8770, 1060, 3495, 8810, 8382}.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
